# L §2.4 (round 17): "Inside a section: its clause lines and notes first, in the grammar's order (§2.2)"; "Clause
# order is the order in the grammar" (a move's on, at, for, when, reads, before/after, ties, attr, leg, fulfils, note;
# a fill's v, note, supply, demand, arc, order; an index's v, assumed, note); round 17's "A regime prints its items in the same kind
# order, ..." (gone in round 19, GD-1: the regime is unboxed, its items top-level sections in kind order). Lines of
# one clause keep their order (the legs and attributes of a kind, a move's legs); a kind's leg, attr and note lines
# are one repeated choice in the grammar (kline), so they keep the file's order too. A blank line separates sections.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

kind trades: event certain
  leg units: notes
  note "a trade"
  leg cash: PLN
  attr seq: int

index ys = 2020..2030
  assumed "a range"
  note "years"
  v v1

move pay[mo in months]: trades
  leg cash from konto to shop amount 2 PLN
  leg units from shop to konto amount n
  note "monthly"
  attr seq = 1
  when c
  on end_of(mo)
  fulfils plan[mo]

fill f
  order b.day
  arc true
  demand d[s] for s in sales
  supply u[b] for b in buys
  note "lots"
  v v1

def tax[p in persons]: money PLN = 0 PLN
place fisc: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rate: num
kind assessments: event certain
  leg tax: PLN
